WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:01.708
- I did it. I finally did it.

00:00:01.791 --> 00:00:03.791
ANDREW REID WON A SUPER BOWL!

00:00:03.958 --> 00:00:06.416
- WOW, WHAT A FUN, EASY SPORT!

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.625
- Goodbye, Gridiron Heights.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.083
It really means a lot to get my own farewell—

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.333
- HI, EVERYONE. 

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.916
MY DAD IS STARTING X-TREME GRIDIRON HEIGHTS! LOL.

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:18.291
- Wait, guys—

00:00:18.416 --> 00:00:19.708
- Eli, man, we’re on to another thing!

00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:21.833
- I’m Oliver Luck, lol. 

00:00:21.958 --> 00:00:23.416
Because everyone's been moving recently—

00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:25.041
- WHAT THE FLUFF IS A CHARGER ANYWAY?

00:00:25.416 --> 00:00:27.041
- I lied to Hulu. I’ll do it. I’ll move. 

00:00:27.166 --> 00:00:29.333
- I don’t think about you as much as you think I do. 

00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:30.875
- Wait, I didn’t know I was moving.

00:00:31.166 --> 00:00:32.291
- We now own the town. 

00:00:32.416 --> 00:00:34.500
Gridiron Heights is X-TREME now!

00:00:34.666 --> 00:00:36.500
- OK, I’m leaving for real—OOOF.

00:00:36.791 --> 00:00:38.291
- DO WHATEVER THE F--K YOU WANT!

00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:40.458
- Everyone calm down. This WILL blow over.

00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:41.708
- WHERE SHOULD I GO?!

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.708
- DERRICK, HERE!

00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:44.041
- Yeah, but do you have enough money, though?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.625
- TAYSOM, we need Drew!

00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:48.208
- Should I save myself? Or is it time to give up? Hmmm…

00:00:48.458 --> 00:00:49.750
- I’m all you need right here, sir.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.416
- Looks like I’m in another classic Zac Taylor scrape!

00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:54.750
- JOE BURROW!

00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:57.125
- [Announcer:] NEXT SEASON, GRIDIRON HEIGHTS WILL COME BACK.

00:00:57.166 --> 00:00:58.291
- [Kyle Shanahan:] NO. NO MORE COMEBACKS.

00:00:58.416 --> 00:00:59.875
NO ONE'S EVER COMING BACK AGAIN.

